   1.  An Introduction
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   UpdateEnglish  was  written  due  to  the  fact  that  Excelsior!   is
   constantly  being  updated,  and  with all of these updates, there are
   usually changes made to the "English" language file.

   Seeing  as  the  English  file has reached 2200+ lines already, it can
   take  a  while to search through and find any changes made for the new
   version.  Also, as most SysOp's will change their English files to add
   support  for  other programs and the like, you can't just copy the new
   English file over the old one easily.

   Therefore,  UpdateEnglish  will  compare  each  line  in two files and
   notify  the  user of any differences.  I have also added the option to
   generate a new file to include which-ever line uou want (see later).



   2.  Requirments
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   UpdateEnglish can be used on any Amiga with V36+, and does not require
   Excelsior! to be running to work.

   UpdateEnglish can also be used on files other than "English" files, as
   it works with standard ASCII text files.



   3.  Usage
   ~~~~~~~~~
   This version of UpdateEnglish can only be used from the SHELL.


   The arguments available are:  OLDFILE/A,NEWFILE/A,TO/K,S=STRIPIPL/S


     OLDFILE    - This is the English file that you are currently working
                  with and want the new file compared with.


     NEWFILE    - This is the New English file.


     TO         - This is an optional filename. If it is specfied, then a
                  file will be generated using the name placed after this
                  keyword.  eg. TO=NewEnglish.temp

                  If  the  TO  option  is  not  present,  then all of the
                  differences  will just be shown to the screen.  This is
                  so  if  you want to write them down, and perhaps change
                  them by hand, you can.

                  When  the  TO is present, a new file will be generated.
                  It  is  created  by copying the lines from the NEW file
                  into  the  TO file, unless there is a difference in the
                  OLD and NEW lines.


                  If  there  is  a  difference  in the lines, you will be
                  presented with a line:  Use line 1, 2 or E >

                  If  `1'  is  selected  or you just hit return, then the
                  line from the OLD file will be copied into the TO file.
                  If  you select `2' then the line from the NEW file will
                  be copied.

                  The  other  option  is  'E'.  This allows you to create
                  your  own  custom line.  This new line may be upto 1024
                  characters long.


   If  the  NEW  file  has  more  lines  than the OLD file, these will be
   automaticly appended to the TO file if it was selected, otherwise they
   are  ignored.   Unfortunally,  if  the OLD file is longer than the NEW
   file,  then  these  extra lines will be ignored, irespective of the TO
   option.


     S=STRIPIPL - This new option causes certain IPL codes to be filtered
                  when doing the comparison of lines.  This means that if
                  the  only  change  you made on a line was to change the
                  colours,  then  the line will not be shown up as having
                  been changed.  At the moment the following codes can be
                  filtered out:   \Cx   \Zx   \Ox   \Rx   \Ux   \Qx



   4.  History
   ~~~~~~~~~~~
   V1.0  12 March 93
       * First release.

   V1.01 12 June 93
       * Modified to handle longer lines
       * Improved code to increase speed and reduce executable size

   V1.02 14 June 93
       * Removed redundant routine
       * Cleaned up text output

   V1.03 1 October 93 <unreleased>
       * Removed need for keyfile.  I had little response from this, so I
         gave  up  on  it.   UpdateEnglish is now un-restricted, but will
         only   be   supported/continued   if  I  do  get  some  form  of
         contributions or donations

   V1.04 7 December 93
       * Totally re-wrote the text output routines
       * Modified general operation in preperation for V2
       * Fixed bug with non release of file handles if there was an error
       * Fixed error that prevented full length custom lines

   V1.05 9 December 93
       * Found a flaw in the write function.  Would not write out any
         lines that weren't different
       ! Found what could be called a bug, but I can't re-create it.
         Sometimes, a line of garbage will be used as the TO savename if
         you didn't specify one.  This is not my fault as far as I can
         tell, but a fault of the compiler.

   V1.06 17 December 93
       * Fixed a minor error that caused an extra un-needed line to be
         printed at the end of the process
       * Changed Version string slightly

   V1.07 21 January 94 <Bitch & Whine release>
       * Added an option to Filter IPL codes from strings when doing
         comparisons.  This was added because one of the users kept
         bugging me to add this option (Hiya R.  :)
       * Cleaned up and edited various text strings displayed
       * Optimized compare routine to speed it up alot

    V1.08 2 February 94
       * There was a problem with the STRIPIPL routine due to the way E
         handled strings differing to the method described in the manual
       * Old lines re-inserted into the TO English file no longer counted
         in the final number of changes reported at the end of the process

    V1.09 13 February 94
       * Now correctly adds lines that passed the check routines once they
         had been stripped using STRIPIPL




   5.  Future
   ~~~~~~~~~~

   Version  2 of UpdateEnglish has been started by myself.

   It will no longer use the Shell for it's output and operation.  I will
   either  do  a  quick  GUI, or maybe just make use of ReqTools/ASL.  It
   will  work  from  Workbench, and also will support more features (like
   Wildcards, file-requestors, logging and whatever else anyone suggests)

   If  you  want  a  version  that  will  still work from the Shell, then
   contact  me fast, before I remove those routines.  If you don't really
   care, then they won't be there for the next release.



